From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MI50 ROCm 10.x project <mi50-rocm10@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] TheRock: keep hipSPARSELt on the gfx906 fallback path

hipSPARSELt's ROCm 10 implementation is a structured-sparse MFMA path and
ships logic only for newer matrix-core targets. Keep it out of the MI50 build
graph so a missing gfx906 kernel cannot be mistaken for a usable feature.
rocSPARSE remains the supported sparse implementation while a future generic
fallback can be developed independently.

---
 cmake/therock_amdgpu_targets.cmake | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/cmake/therock_amdgpu_targets.cmake b/cmake/therock_amdgpu_targets.cmake
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/cmake/therock_amdgpu_targets.cmake
+++ b/cmake/therock_amdgpu_targets.cmake
@@ -87,7 +87,6 @@ if(MI50_ENABLE_FORWARD_PORTS)
   list(REMOVE_ITEM _gfx906_excluded_projects
     hipBLASLt
-    hipSPARSELt
     composable_kernel
     hipTensor
   )
 endif()
--
